# Ohm standard library — the component-type taxonomy (std.kinds, ADR-008)
#
# A `kind` is a checkable CONTRACT for a category of part: the pins (by role) and
# params EVERY in-production member genuinely has. A component declares the kinds
# it IS (`component TLV9061(OpAmp):`) and binds each required member to a pin
# (`pin OUT: role=output, pad=1, is=out`); the compiler verifies conformance.
#
# HONESTY / OPEN-WORLD (N3):
#   * `requires` is adversarially MINIMAL — only what NO real member lacks. Things
#     that vary (op-amp V-, LDO EN, shunt-ref supply, 4-terminal MOSFET body) are
#     `optional`, never required, so a legitimate part never false-fails.
#   * A component with NO declared kind is the base `Component` — unchecked. The
#     taxonomy never claims to enumerate every device; unknown = unasserted.
#   * IS-A refinement (Schottky(Diode)) is a shallow single spine; capabilities
#     (ThermalPad, ExposedPad) are orthogonal kinds that compose freely.

# ---------- passives ----------
kind TwoTerminal:
    requires a: passive
    requires b: passive

# defining param names match the library's attr convention (`value`, `freq`), so
# a retrofit `component Resistor(Resistor)` with `value=10kohm` conforms directly.
kind Resistor(TwoTerminal):
    param value: resistance

kind Capacitor(TwoTerminal):
    param value: capacitance

kind Inductor(TwoTerminal):
    param value: inductance

kind Crystal(TwoTerminal):
    param freq: frequency

# ---------- diodes (polar two-terminal spine) ----------
# Vf/Vz/Vbr vary in how they're specified and are often left to the datasheet, so
# they are NOT required params — the subtypes just refine the pin contract.
kind Diode:
    requires anode: passive
    requires cathode: passive

kind Zener(Diode)

kind Schottky(Diode)

kind LED(Diode)

kind TVS(Diode)

# ---------- transistors ----------
kind BJT:
    requires base: input
    requires collector: passive
    requires emitter: passive

kind MOSFET:
    requires gate: input
    requires drain: passive
    requires source: passive
    optional body: passive        # brought out only on 4-terminal parts

kind JFET:
    requires gate: input
    requires drain: passive
    requires source: passive

# ---------- analog ICs ----------
kind OpAmp:
    requires inp: input
    requires inn: input
    requires out: output
    requires vpos: power_in
    optional vneg: power_in       # single-supply parts omit — NOT required

kind Comparator:
    requires inp: input
    requires inn: input
    requires out: output          # push-pull; open-collector parts override role=open_collector
    requires vpos: power_in
    optional vneg: power_in

kind VoltageReference:
    requires out: output          # shunt refs are 2-terminal + ref; supply is optional
    optional vpos: power_in

# ---------- power ICs ----------
kind LDO:
    requires vin: power_in
    requires vout: power_out
    requires gnd: ground
    optional en: input            # fixed 3-pin LDOs have none

kind SwitchingConverter:
    requires vin: power_in
    requires gnd: ground
    requires sw: output           # controllers (no integrated switch) are a distinct kind

# ---------- logic / interface ----------
kind LogicGate:
    requires out: output
    requires vcc: power_in
    requires gnd: ground

kind Buffer(LogicGate):
    requires inp: input

kind Transceiver:
    requires vcc: power_in
    requires gnd: ground

# ---------- misc ----------
kind Oscillator:
    requires out: output
    requires vcc: power_in
    requires gnd: ground

kind Optocoupler:
    requires led_anode: input
    requires led_cathode: passive

kind Relay:
    requires coil_a: input
    requires coil_b: passive
    requires com: passive

kind Fuse(TwoTerminal)

# A connector is a mechanical mating interface; electrically its pins are
# role-agnostic. The only universal is "has at least one contact" — so no
# required members here (extends the open base).
kind Connector:
    optional shield: ground

# A sensor's only near-universal is "produces a signal"; supply is NOT universal
# (thermocouples, photodiodes, piezo are self-powered).
kind Sensor:
    requires signal: output

# ---------- orthogonal capabilities (compose with any kind) ----------
kind ThermalPad:
    requires ep: passive

kind ExposedPad:
    requires ep: passive

kind Shielded:
    requires shield: ground
